1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,833
You know, a very bad person
invented trigonometry.

2
00:00:02,833 --> 00:00:04,083
Can I drive to school today?

3
00:00:04,083 --> 00:00:05,750
What? I'm a good driver.

4
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:06,458
Have a good day.

5
00:00:06,458 --> 00:00:07,083
Have fun.

6
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,208
See you guys later.

7
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:09,208
I'll let you drive.

8
00:00:09,208 --> 00:00:13,000
Hey, so, you wanna go
for a climb after school?

9
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:17,708
Yeah, I was kinda thinking I might
go over to Brooke's after school.

10
00:00:17,708 --> 00:00:19,500
How's that going with her, by the way?

11
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,750
I don't know.

12
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,250
Why don't you just tell her?

13
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:24,583
Does Brooke even know that you like her?

14
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,542
What if she likes Drew?

15
00:00:26,542 --> 00:00:29,750
Then you know the score,
that she has bad taste.

16
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,667
- Hey. Where are you?

17
00:00:30,667 --> 00:00:33,167
Yeah, I was driving myself to school.

18
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,292
Oh, God. Jason, this is
a little bit weird.

19
00:00:35,292 --> 00:00:36,833
It should be you. You know this.

20
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:39,292
Don't worry about them. Just-- You do you.

21
00:00:39,292 --> 00:00:40,792
What's that supposed to be?

22
00:00:40,792 --> 00:00:44,792
You have a cat in a sealed box.

23
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:48,917
And also in the box,
we have a vial of poison,

24
00:00:48,917 --> 00:00:52,625
Now, if there's no atomic decay,
the cat lives.

25
00:00:52,625 --> 00:00:57,958
Before we look inside,
the atom exists in a superposition,

26
00:00:57,958 --> 00:00:59,417
Which means what?

27
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,333
This guy had a thing for torturing cats.

28
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,542
and he had a thing
for understanding the universe.

29
00:01:03,542 --> 00:01:07,833
The answer, for anybody who cares to know,
is that the atom in superposition

30
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:11,958
means that the cat is both alive
and it is dead.

31
00:01:11,958 --> 00:01:13,333
His name's Woody Gwyn,

32
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:15,875
one of America's
great contemporary landscape masters.

33
00:01:15,875 --> 00:01:17,042
- Let me get my stuff.

34
00:01:17,042 --> 00:01:17,833
- I could paint that.

35
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:19,167
- You can do anything, babe.

36
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:21,667
I'm apartment hunting Friday,
if you wanna come.

37
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:25,792
I would love to,
but Friday is my training day.

38
00:01:25,792 --> 00:01:29,458
My cycling time and my running time
aren't bad actually,

39
00:01:29,458 --> 00:01:31,000
but my swimming really needs work.

40
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,500
And right now, I can't even imagine
doing them all back-to-back.

41
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,583
You know, there are less agonizing ways
for you to avoid your family.

42
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:39,708
- I'm just saying.
- I'm not avoiding them.

43
00:01:39,708 --> 00:01:40,875
- So, when's the race?

44
00:01:40,875 --> 00:01:42,917
Well, I think it would be foolish not to.

45
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:44,417
That's why I love you.

46
00:01:44,417 --> 00:01:47,083
'Cause I'm an advocate
of opening more wine always?

47
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:49,292
That's the source
of your adoration for me?

48
00:01:49,292 --> 00:01:51,542
Yeah, I think that's the only reason
we've made it this far.

49
00:01:51,542 --> 00:01:52,500
Close your eyes.

50
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:53,792
Your phone's blowing up.

51
00:01:53,792 --> 00:01:54,625
- Who is it?

52
00:01:54,625 --> 00:01:57,583
and he's wondering where you are?

53
00:01:57,583 --> 00:01:58,875
- I found out today.

54
00:01:58,875 --> 00:02:00,042
Where is it happening?

55
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:04,875
Because he knows that if he picks
any place remotely far away, I'm not gonna show.

56
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:06,500
I'm glad you're having a good time. No.

57
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,208
You know he would show up for you.

58
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:13,792
You're having a little celebration
at my local bar, then it's probably - a desperate plea for my attention.

59
00:02:13,792 --> 00:02:16,708
Your wife is a beautiful genius,
and I appreciate her.

60
00:02:16,708 --> 00:02:17,875
Congratulations.

61
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:20,708
Could I
introduce you to a bunch of people?

62
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:22,042
The kind you don't really wanna meet.

63
00:02:22,042 --> 00:02:23,167
And what do you do?

64
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:25,000
- I teach physics at Lakemont.

65
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,750
What exactly was the citation again?

66
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,208
And don't pretend
you haven't memorized it.

67
00:02:30,208 --> 00:02:31,167
I owe you.

68
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:37,958
We're scientists. We sign on
to struggle and search our entire lives in anonymity, you know?

69
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:39,542
Congratulations.

70
00:02:39,542 --> 00:02:41,542
It wasn't for some bullshit victory lap.

71
00:02:41,542 --> 00:02:43,292
Jason, we already have the space.

72
00:02:43,292 --> 00:02:45,083
I'm really gonna have to get back
to them actually.

73
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:47,042
if you don't do exactly what I say,

74
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:48,167
I will kill you.

75
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:51,250
Eyes on the road. Keep driving.

76
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,042
What's the passcode to your phone?

77
00:02:53,042 --> 00:02:54,250
What kind of job?

78
00:02:54,292 --> 00:02:57,958
He's starting a neurotech company
in San Francisco.

79
00:02:58,042 --> 00:02:58,875
- What did you say?

80
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:00,583
- Well, I didn't give him an answer.

81
00:03:00,583 --> 00:03:01,500
Take this exit.

82
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,667
Take off your clothes.

83
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:03,500
Start moving.

84
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,542
Down there.
